        "body": "## Summary\n\nFull implementation of all 20 items (E01–E20) from the ChatPanel audit plan, targeting 10/10 quality on the ChatPanel module.\n\n### Contact Ref & Disambiguation (E01–E03)\n- **E01** — New `src/features/inbox/utils/contactRef.ts`: `resolveContactRef()` utility disambiguates UUID (`contacts.id`) from WhatsApp JID (`xxx@s.whatsapp.net`), preventing the PostgREST 400 \"invalid input syntax for type uuid\" that silently broke external-mode conversations.\n- **E02** — `useFallbackContact.ts`: now routes by `ref.kind` — `'uuid'` → `contacts.eq('id', ...)`, `'jid'` → `evolution_contacts.eq('remote_jid', ...)`; logs warning on failure instead of silently returning null.\n- **E03** — `useChatPanelHandlers.ts`: `instanceName` propagated as explicit param; edit-message pre-condition guard with destructive toast when `instanceName`/`externalId`/`targetJid` are absent; WhatsApp API called first, DB update only on success.\n\n### Virtualised Scroll (E04, E16)\n- **E04 / E16** — `ChatMessagesArea.tsx` + `VirtualizedMessageList.tsx`: `measureElement` for real height measurement; `scrollToMessage` via index map + `virtualizer.scrollToIndex`; `useImperativeHandle` exposes `{scrollToBottom, scrollToMessage}`; stable `getItemKey`.\n\n### Realtime Channel (E05)\n- **E05** — `ChatMessagesArea.tsx`: channel named `chat-updates:${contactJid}` (per-conversation), replacing shared fixed-name channel.\n\n### Database / Security (E06–E10)\n- **E06** — Migration `20260731000001`: idempotent `DO $$ … $$` assertion that `evo.evolution_messages` root (not leaf partitions) is in `supabase_realtime` publication.\n- **E07** — `useExternalApiManagement.ts`: `effectiveInstance` computed from `instanceName ?? DEFAULT_INSTANCE`; used in cache keys and all `useEffect` deps.\n- **E08** *(Phase 1)* — Migration `20260731000002`: `v_rls_impact_preview` view enumerates policies that would need update before Phase 3 RLS hardening is applied.\n- **E09** — Migration `20260731000003`: `REVOKE TRUNCATE ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA zapp FROM authenticated, anon` — prevents destructive truncation by app-level roles.\n- **E10** — Migration `20260731000004`: `REVOKE SELECT ON zapp.profiles, zapp.workspace_members, zapp.user_roles FROM anon` — no anon enumeration of personal data.\n\n### Edit / Signature / Contract (E11–E13)\n- **E11** — Edit message guard (see E03).\n- **E12** — `useMessageSignature.applySignature`: early return `if (content.startsWith(prefix)) return content` — idempotent on retry.\n- **E13** — `ChatPanelProps.onSendMessage` and `UseProductHandlersOptions.onSendMessage` both updated to the 3-param contract: `(content: string, attachments?: File[], onProgress?: (p: number) => void) => void | Promise<void>`.\n\n### UUID Guards for Auxiliary Inserts (E14)\n- **E14** — `CloseConversationDialog.tsx`: `isValidUUID(contactId)` guard before `conversation_closures` INSERT — shows descriptive toast for external-mode contacts instead of a silent PostgREST 400. `useRemindersData.createReminder`: same guard at the data layer, consistent with the existing `fetchReminders` guard.\n\n### Performance (E15)\n- **E15** — `useChatFilters.ts`: all 4 derived values (`failedMessages`, `categoryCounts`, `categoryFilteredMessages`, `visibleMessages`) wrapped in `useMemo`; `categoryCounts` uses a single-pass `for` loop instead of 3 `.filter()` passes.\n\n### Dead Code / Duplication (E17, E18)\n- **E17** — `ChatPanel.tsx`: duplicate `useQuickReplies()` call removed; dead `useMemo` vars (`_canGenerateSummary`, `_lastContactMessages`, `_allMessagesForHeader`) deleted.\n- **E18** — `src/features/inbox/components/chat/useChatPanel.ts` (superseded dead-code file) deleted.\n\n### Tests (E19)\n- **E19** — `src/features/inbox/components/chat/__tests__/p0-regressions.test.ts` (568 lines): regression guards for contactRef routing, fallback contact, scrollToMessage, edit-message guard, and filter identity stability.\n\n### CI / Lint (E20)\n- **E20** — `.github/workflows/db-invariants.yml`: 5-invariant DB check (no leaf+parent in publication, no TRUNCATE for app roles, no anon SELECT on personal data, no USING(true) enumeration policies, all bridge views have `security_invoker`). `eslint.config.js`: rules against hardcoded `'wpp2'` literals and fixed-name Realtime channels.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npx tsc --noEmit --skipLibCheck` — 0 errors\n- [x] All 20 items verified implemented or pre-existing in DB (confirmed via Supabase self-hosted diagnostic queries)\n- [x] `useChatPanelHandlers.ts` whisper UUID guard: `isValidUUID(contactId)` before INSERT\n- [x] `CloseConversationDialog.tsx` UUID guard: descriptive toast for JID contacts\n- [x] `createReminder`: UUID guard at data layer\n- [x] Channel naming per-conversation: `chat-updates:${contactJid}`\n- [x] Signature idempotency: `applySignature('')` returns `''` on retry\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nCompletes the 20-item ChatPanel audit to improve reliability, security, and performance. Tightens contact handling, streamlines message sending and scrolling, and hardens DB and CI safeguards.\n\n- **New Features**\n  - Accurate virtualized list with `scrollToMessage` and `scrollToBottom`.\n  - Per-conversation realtime channel `chat-updates:${contactJid}`.\n  - Unified send contract: `(content, attachments?, onProgress?)` for all handlers.\n  - Contact ref resolver distinguishes UUIDs from WhatsApp JIDs.\n\n- **Security**\n  - UUID guards before inserting into `conversation_closures` and `reminders`.\n  - DB migrations restrict `TRUNCATE` and `anon` `SELECT`, and ensure `evo.evolution_messages` is in `supabase_realtime`.\n  - CI adds DB invariants; ESLint blocks hardcoded instance names and shared channels.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 197c54d7a7b63330f597c3ea4cd5ebec0eef76ec. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/adm01-debug/zapp-web-v3/pull/632?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n",
